# Marquise Cut Diamond Size Chart ({{year}}): Face-Up MM by Carat vs Round

![Marquise diamond size chart showing three marquise cut diamonds held in tweezers against a soft grey background, used as the hero image for the DiamondCritics {{year}} marquise cut diamond size chart guide](/images/marquise-cut-diamond-size-chart.jpg "Marquise Cut Diamond Size Chart 3 Carat Weights That Fool Buyers")

## TL;DR — The Marquise Diamond Size Chart in One Scroll

A **marquise diamond size chart** maps carat weight to face-up millimetres. The short answer: at the same carat, a marquise looks 10–25% bigger than a round. The illusion peaks around 1.5ct, then fades fast above 2.5ct.

**The 3 carat weights that fool buyers (full breakdown further down):**

- **The 0.75ct Ghost.** A 0.75ct marquise is ~9.5 × 4.75 mm. On a size-6 finger it reads almost identical to a 1ct round. You can save $400–$900 and nobody can tell.
- **The 1.5ct Peak.** A 1.5ct marquise hits ~12 × 6 mm — longer than a 2ct round and wider on the long axis. This is the single biggest size-per-dollar sweet spot in the chart.
- **The 3ct Letdown.** A 3ct marquise is only ~7.5 mm wide. Buyers expect "big" and get "long." It covers less finger side-to-side than a 2ct round.

→ Our pick for size-per-dollar: **[1ct H-VS2 Ideal Cut marquise at $4,393](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/30259333?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** — 10 × 5 mm face-up, reads as 1.25ct round on the finger.

**Priority:** length-to-width ratio decides the size illusion. A 2.00 L:W reads 20% longer than a 1.75 L:W at the same carat. If finger coverage matters more than width, buy ratio first, carat second.

## Expert Summary

A marquise diamond size chart has to show two numbers per carat — the length and the width — because the marquise face-up is an ellipse, not a circle. At 1ct, the standard measurement is **10.0 × 5.0 mm** at a 2.00 length-to-width ratio. That is 54% longer than a 1ct round (6.5 mm) but 23% narrower.

The size illusion is real but it has a ceiling. From 0.5ct to about 1.75ct, marquise reads bigger on the finger than a round of the same weight. From 2.5ct up, the width stops growing fast enough to match buyer expectations for a "statement" stone. I'm Farzana Hasan, a GIA-certified diamond expert, and this is the chart I show every client who thinks a 3ct marquise will look like a 3ct round. Full credentials at **[Diamond Critics](https://diamondcritics.com/about-farzana/)**.

This guide covers face-up mm at every carat from 0.5 to 5ct, side-by-side round comparisons, finger coverage percentages, and the three carat weights where the illusion either delivers extraordinary value or quietly fails. Prices come from current certified market inventory. Our full **[marquise cut diamond guide](/marquise-cut-diamond)** covers the pillar fundamentals.

